@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam classBackgroundColor #F8F9FA
skinparam classBorderColor #6C757D
skinparam arrowColor #495057
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

actor User
participant "Frontend\n(Export Modal)" as Frontend
participant "Backend API" as Backend
participant "Export Service" as Export
participant WeasyPrint
database Database

== Preview ==
User -> Frontend : Open Export Modal and select settings
Frontend -> Backend : GET /projects/{project_id}/documents/{document_id}/export-preview
Backend -> Database : Load document, project, sections
Backend -> Export : export_html(sections, document, project, settings)
Export -> Export : Render Markdown sections to HTML
Export -> Export : Apply CSS export settings
Export --> Backend : HTML string
Backend --> Frontend : text/html
Frontend --> User : Render HTML in iframe

== PDF Export ==
User -> Frontend : Click Export PDF
Frontend -> Backend : GET /projects/{project_id}/documents/{document_id}/export?format=pdf
Backend -> Database : Load document, project, sections
Backend -> Export : export_pdf(sections, document, project, settings)
Export -> Export : Render HTML
Export -> WeasyPrint : HTML(string=html).write_pdf()
WeasyPrint --> Export : PDF bytes
Export --> Backend : PDF binary
Backend --> Frontend : application/pdf attachment
Frontend --> User : Trigger file download

== Batch Export ==
User -> Frontend : Select multiple projects and batch export
Frontend -> Backend : POST /projects/batch-export
Backend -> Database : Load selected projects and first documents
loop each project/document
  Backend -> Export : export_pdf(sections, document, project, settings)
  Export -> WeasyPrint : write_pdf()
  WeasyPrint --> Export : PDF bytes
  Export --> Backend : PDF binary
end
Backend -> Backend : Package PDFs into ZIP
Backend --> Frontend : application/zip attachment
Frontend --> User : Trigger ZIP download
@enduml
